      "id": "overview",
      "title": "One build, end to end",
      "question": "Which parts does one build pass through, from the author's model to a published delivery?",
      "summary": "The author runs archpub build, and the delivery builder makes plates, the print edition and the page. The reviewer runs accept and publish; the acceptance stage copies only an accepted delivery to the publication root.",
